{"uuid": "1266c807-3d95-477e-9a2b-73c8bd812f69", "status": true, "parsed": {"nodes": [{"id": "H1", "content": "The reaction involves a free radical transformation process where air (O2) acts as an oxidant/initiator", "type": "MECHANISM_STEP", "ability_tags": ["2.2 Reaction Pathway & Intermediate Identification", "2.3 Reaction Mechanism & Kinetic Interpretation"]}, {"id": "H2", "content": "The main product A has the structure (4-Cl)C6H4-CH=C(C#N)-C(=O)-NH-(p-tolyl)", "type": "STRUCTURE_ID", "ability_tags": ["2.4 Product Structure Prediction"]}, {"id": "H3", "content": "The side product B has the structure (4-Cl)C6H4-CH=CH-C(=O)-C(=O)-NH-(p-tolyl)", "type": "STRUCTURE_ID", "ability_tags": ["2.4 Product Structure Prediction"]}, {"id": "H4", "content": "The side product B has the molecular formula C17H14ClNO2", "type": "STRUCTURE_ID", "ability_tags": ["2.1 Chemical Equation & Stoichiometry"]}, {"id": "H5", "content": "Option C is the correct answer", "type": "OPTION_JUDGMENT", "ability_tags": ["2.4 Product Structure Prediction"]}], "edges": [{"from": "H1", "to": "H2"}, {"from": "H1", "to": "H3"}, {"from": "H2", "to": "H5"}, {"from": "H3", "to": "H5"}, {"from": "H4", "to": "H3"}], "matches": [{"h_id": "H1", "r_id": "R1"}, {"h_id": "H2", "r_id": null}, {"h_id": "H3", "r_id": "R6"}, {"h_id": "H4", "r_id": null}, {"h_id": "H5", "r_id": null}]}}
{"uuid": "72933c79-dddb-4483-9d32-39503bff0ff1", "status": true, "parsed": {"nodes": [{"id": "H1", "content": "Reaction 1 involves the addition of methyl Grignard reagent (C[Mg]Br) to the ester group", "type": "MECHANISM_STEP", "ability_tags": ["2.5 Functional Group Transformation & Protection", "2.2 Reaction Pathway & Intermediate Identification"]}, {"id": "H2", "content": "The ester group is converted into a tertiary alcohol, forming product A", "type": "MECHANISM_STEP", "ability_tags": ["2.4 Product Structure Prediction", "2.5 Functional Group Transformation & Protection"]}, {"id": "H3", "content": "Reaction 2 is an acid-catalyzed intramolecular cyclization involving dehydration of the tertiary alcohol to a carbocation", "type": "MECHANISM_STEP", "ability_tags": ["2.3 Reaction Mechanism & Kinetic Interpretation", "2.2 Reaction Pathway & Intermediate Identification"]}, {"id": "H4", "content": "The dehydration forms a stable tertiary carbocation on the side chain", "type": "MECHANISM_STEP", "ability_tags": ["2.2 Reaction Pathway & Intermediate Identification", "1.6 Bonding Pattern & Electronic Effect Analysis"]}, {"id": "H5", "content": "The double bond in the six-membered ring attacks the carbocation intramolecularly", "type": "MECHANISM_STEP", "ability_tags": ["2.2 Reaction Pathway & Intermediate Identification", "2.3 Reaction Mechanism & Kinetic Interpretation"]}, {"id": "H6", "content": "This cyclization forms a new five-membered ring", "type": "MECHANISM_STEP", "ability_tags": ["2.4 Product Structure Prediction", "1.1 Molecular Geometry & Symmetry Analysis"]}, {"id": "H7", "content": "The key intermediate corresponds to the structure in Option D", "type": "STRUCTURE_ID", "ability_tags": ["2.4 Product Structure Prediction", "1.1 Molecular Geometry & Symmetry Analysis"]}, {"id": "H8", "content": "Option D is correct", "type": "OPTION_JUDGMENT", "ability_tags": ["2.4 Product Structure Prediction", "1.1 Molecular Geometry & Symmetry Analysis"]}, {"id": "H9", "cont