{"uuid": "cde4b445-eef4-4150-90b1-d878c004d822", "status": true, "parsed": {"nodes": [{"id": "H1", "content": "The molar ratio of Mo to N in X is approximately 4:3", "type": "NUMERIC_VALUE", "ability_tags": ["2.1 Chemical Equation & Stoichiometry"]}, {"id": "H2", "content": "The molar ratio of O to N in X is approximately 5:1", "type": "NUMERIC_VALUE", "ability_tags": ["2.1 Chemical Equation & Stoichiometry"]}, {"id": "H3", "content": "The chemical formula of X is C_{49}H_{110}N_3Mo_4O_{15} with anion [Mo_4O_{15}(CH_2)]^{3-}", "type": "STRUCTURE_ID", "ability_tags": ["1.4 Coordination Compound Structure & Bonding", "2.4 Product Structure Prediction"]}, {"id": "H4", "content": "Statement 1 is correct because H count is 110", "type": "OPTION_JUDGMENT", "ability_tags": ["2.1 Chemical Equation & Stoichiometry"]}, {"id": "H5", "content": "The reaction produces [(n-C_4H_9)_4N]OH (TBAOH)", "type": "MECHANISM_STEP", "ability_tags": ["2.4 Product Structure Prediction"]}, {"id": "H6", "content": "Statement 2 is incorrect because the solution is basic", "type": "OPTION_JUDGMENT", "ability_tags": ["4.2 Interpretation & Inference of Experimental Phenomena"]}, {"id": "H7", "content": "The anion structure is [Mo_4O_{15}(CH_2)]^{3-} containing 2 triply coordinated O", "type": "STRUCTURE_ID", "ability_tags": ["1.4 Coordination Compound Structure & Bonding"]}, {"id": "H8", "content": "Statement 3 is correct", "type": "OPTION_JUDGMENT", "ability_tags": ["1.4 Coordination Compound Structure & Bonding"]}, {"id": "H9", "content": "In molybdates, Mo atoms usually have no more than 2 terminal oxygen atoms", "type": "PROPERTY_ASSERTION", "ability_tags": ["1.7 Structure-Property Correlation & Prediction"]}, {"id": "H10", "content": "Statement 4 is correct", "type": "OPTION_JUDGMENT", "ability_tags": ["1.7 Structure-Property Correlation & Prediction"]}, {"id": "H11", "content": "Option N (1, 3, 4) is correct", "type": "OPTION_JUDGMENT", "ability_tags": []}], "edges": [{"from": "H1", "to": "H3