{"uuid": "7e72890a-387d-41a2-9121-ea827f0bc4d2", "status": true, "parsed": {"nodes": [{"id": "H1", "content": "Derive equilibrium relation: $[\\text{HO}_2^-] = \\frac{K_2}{K_w} [\\text{H}_2\\text{O}_2][\\text{OH}^-]$", "type": "PROPERTY_ASSERTION", "ability_tags": ["3.3 Chemical Equilibrium Principle & Shift Analysis", "3.4 Equilibrium Constant & System Calculation"]}, {"id": "H2", "content": "Derive steady-state $[\\text{HO}\\cdot] = \\sqrt{\\frac{k_3[\\text{O}_3][\\text{HO}_2^-]}{2k_{12}}}$", "type": "PROPERTY_ASSERTION", "ability_tags": ["2.3 Reaction Mechanism & Kinetic Interpretation", "3.7 Chemical Kinetics Theory & Rate Law"]}, {"id": "H3", "content": "Derive steady-state $[\\text{O}_2^-] = \\frac{k_3 K_2}{k_9 K_w} [\\text{H}_2\\text{O}_2][\\text{OH}^-]$", "type": "PROPERTY_ASSERTION", "ability_tags": ["2.3 Reaction Mechanism & Kinetic Interpretation", "3.7 Chemical Kinetics Theory & Rate Law"]}, {"id": "H4", "content": "Derive ozone consumption rate $v_{\\text{O}_3} = (k_1)[\\text{O}_3][\\text{OH}^-] + \\left(\\frac{2k_3 K_2}{K_w}\\right)[\\text{O}_3][\\text{H}_2\\text{O}_2][\\text{OH}^-] + \\left(k_4\\sqrt{\\frac{k_3 K_2}{2k_{12}K_w}}\\right)[\\text{O}_3]^{3/2}[\\text{H}_2\\text{O}_2]^{1/2}[\\text{OH}^-]^{1/2}$", "type": "PROPERTY_ASSERTION", "ability_tags": ["2.3 Reaction Mechanism & Kinetic Interpretation", "3.7 Chemical Kinetics Theory & Rate Law", "3.8 Reaction Rate & Activation Energy Calculation"]}, {"id": "H5", "content": "The expression for $[\\text{O}_2^-]$ includes 1 term", "type": "PROPERTY_ASSERTION", "ability_tags": []}, {"id": "H6", "content": "The expression for $v_{\\text{O}_3}$ includes 3 terms", "type": "PROPERTY_ASSERTION", "ability_tags": []}, {"id": "H7", "content": "Option B is correct", "type": "OPTION_JUDGMENT", "ability_tags": ["2.3 Reaction Mechanism & Kinetic Interpretation", "3.7 Chemical Kinetics Theory & Rate Law"]}], "edges": [{"from": "H1", "to": "H2"}, {"from": "H1", "to": "H3"}, {"from": "H2", "to": "H4"}, {"from": "H3", "to": "H4"}, {"from": "H3", "to": "H5"}, {"from": "H4", "to": "H6"}, {"from": "H5", "to": "H7"}, {"from": "H6", "to": "H7"}], "matches": [{"h_id": "H1", "r_id": null}, {"h_id": "H2", "r_id": null}, {"h_id": "H3", "r_id": null}, {"h_id": "H4", "r_id": null}, {"h_id": "H5", "r_id": null}, {"h_id": "H6", "r_id": null}, {"h_id": "H7", "r_id": null}]}}
{"uuid": "05ba7cae-3682-44dd-9018-f1bff6001ef3", "status": true, "parsed": {"nodes": [{"id": "H1", "content": "Compound C is formed from the initiator radical and dithiobenzoate group, containing 11 carbon atoms, so Statement 1 is correct", "type": "OPTION_JUDGMENT", "ability_tags": ["1.1 Molecular Geometry & Symmetry Analysis", "2.4 Product Structure Prediction"]}, {"id": "H2", "content": "Radical D is the PEG radical and does not contain sulfur atoms, so Statement 2 is incorrect", "type": "OPTION_JUDGMENT", "ability_tags": ["1.1 Molecular Geometry & Symmetry Analysis"]}, {"id": "H3", "content": "Segment z is hydrophilic while segment x is hydrophobic and forms the membrane, so Statement 3 is incorrect", "type": "OPTION_JUDGMENT", "ability_tags": ["1.7 Structure-Property Correlation & Prediction"]}, {"id": "H4", "content": "Increasing the degree of polymerization of segment x increases the density of pH-responsive groups and drug release rate, so Statement 4 is correct", "type": "OPTION_JUDGMENT", "ability_tags": ["1.7 Structure-Property Correlation & Prediction", "2.8 Reaction Condition Optimization & Impact Assessment"]}, {"id": "H5", "content": "Increasing the degree of polymerization of hydrophobic segment y increases stability and decreases release rate, so Statement 5 is incorrect", "type": "OPTION_JUDGMENT", "ability_tags": ["1.7 Structure-Property Correlation & Prediction"]}, {"id": "H6", "content": "Statement 6 is considered incorrect in the context of the available options and the directness of the effect compared to segment x", "type": "OPTION_JUDGMENT", "ability_tags": []}, {"id": "H7", "content": "DEAEMA is more basic than the monomer of segment x (DIPEMA) due to less steric hindrance", "type": "PROPERTY_ASSERTION", "ability_tags": ["1.6 Bonding Pattern & Electronic Effect Analysis"]}, {"id": "H8", "content": "Replacing the monomer of segment x with DEAEMA increases the pH value for drug release, so Statement 7 is correct", "type": "OPTION_JUDGMENT", "ability_tags": ["1.7 Structure-Property Correlation & Prediction"]}, {"id": "H9", "content": "The correct statements are 1, 4, 7, corresponding to Option B", "type": "OPTION_JUDGMENT", "ability_tags": []}], "edges": [{"from": "H7", "to": "H8"}, {"from": "H1", "to": "H9"}, {"from": "H2", "to": "H9"}, {"from": "H3", "to": "H9"}, {"from": "H4", "to": "H9"}, {"from": "H5", "to": "H9"}, {"from": "H6", "to": "H9"}, {"from": "H8", "to": "H9"}], "matches": [{"h_id": "H1", "r_id": "R1"}, {"h_id": "H2", "r_id": "R2"}, {"h_id": "H3", "r_id": "R3"}, {"h_id": "H4", "r_id": "R4"}, {"h_id": "H5", "r_id": "R4"}, {"h_id": "H6", "r_id": "R4"}, {"h_id": "H7", "r_id": "R5"}, {"h_id": "H8", "r_id": "R6"}, {"h_id": "H9", "r_id": "R7"}]}}
